    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nSurround\n\n### Description\n\nMiniSurround does not properly match surrounding characters when using the replace command. It seems to get confused with the next line. For example, when using sr\"', the following issue occurs:\r\n\r\n##### Initial content:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n| vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme\" }, \r\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme\" },\r\n```\r\n\r\n##### After using sr\"':\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme' }, \r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme\" },\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.1 Build type: RelWithDebInfo LuaJIT 2.1.1720049189\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHere’s the corrected and formatted version:\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -u minimal.lua`\r\n2. `lua require(\"mini.surround\").setup()`\r\n3. Open empty files and write the following:\r\n    ```lua\r\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme\" },\r\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"VimResume\", \"ColorScheme\" },\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n4. Move the cursor to the beginning and try to replace `\"` with `'`.\r\n5. Notice the broken behavior.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe surrounding characters should be replaced correctly, so `\"VimEnter\"` should become `'VimEnter'`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/06c76d9d-2d58-4c4c-8db3-53d24998fbae\r\n\r\n",
