        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Interesting, I can reproduce with the above example but also with more complex ones e.g.:\r\n\r\nThe initial issue was \"Move the cursor to the beginning and try to replace `\"` with `'`.\". It explicitly works in demo the way you described as expected behavior.\r\n\r\nAll other cases work as expected and [as documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-surround.txt#L522-L525). Searching is performed in these steps until the first success:\r\n- Try finding covering surrounding in current line.\r\n- Try finding next surrounding in current line.\r\n- Try finding covering surrounding in the whole neighborhood (current line plus `config.n_lines` before and after0.\r\n- Try finding next surrounding in the whole neighborhood.\r\n- Say that nothing can be found.\r\n\r\nEach example in the demo works like this. The quotes are not checked for being balanced before/after, they are just another surrounding pair (same as `(` / `)`, etc.).",
